# The running system is WSL2/Linux; the editing machine is Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true. Without this, git checks out the shell scripts and the
# Makefile with CRLF and Linux refuses to run them:
#
#   /bin/sh^M: bad interpreter
#
# which fails on the demo machine and nowhere else -- the worst place to find it.
# `text=auto` normalises on commit (the blobs are already LF); `eol=lf` makes the
# working tree LF on Windows too, so what is edited is what runs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Nothing in this repo is binary, so nothing gets the `binary` treatment, and a
# `.png` added later should be an explicit decision rather than a silent one.
